{"id":"123","t":"Calculus — Limits & Differentiation","s":"m","v":1,"a":123,"z":139,"sheets":[["img/123-g0.webp",849,4288]],"st":[[20,"Limit of a continuous function (2","","f continuous at (a, b) ⇒ lim<sub>(x,y)→(a,b)</sub> f(x, y) = f(a, b)",1485,1525],[21,"Standard limits","e ≈ 2.718","lim<sub>x→0</sub> sin x / x = 1; lim (1 + 1/n)<sup>n</sup> = e; lim<sub>x→0</sub> (a<sup>x</sup> − 1)/x = ln a; lim<sub>x→0</sub> (e<sup>x</sup> − 1)/x = 1",1485,1525],[22,"L&#x27;Hospital&#x27;s rule","f′ = derivative of f","lim f/g = lim f′/g′ (for 0/0 or ∞/∞)",1485,1525],[23,"Derivatives table","d = d/dx","d(x<sup>n</sup>) = nx<sup>n−1</sup>; d(e<sup>x</sup>) = e<sup>x</sup>; d(ln x) = 1/x; d(a<sup>x</sup>) = a<sup>x</sup> ln a",1485,1525],[24,"Trig derivatives","","d(sin x) = cos x; d(cos x) = −sin x; d(tan x) = sec²x; d(cot x) = −cosec²x; d(sec x) = sec x tan x; d(cosec x) = −cosec x cot x",1485,1525],[25,"Inverse trig derivatives","","d/dx(sin⁻¹x) = 1/√(1 − x²); d/dx(cos⁻¹x) = −1/√(1 − x²); d/dx(tan⁻¹x) = 1/(1 + x²)",1485,1525],[26,"Product, quotient, chain rules","u, v = functions of x","(uv)′ = u′v + uv′; (u/v)′ = (u′v − uv′)/v²; dy/dx = dy/du · du/dx",1485,1525],[27,"Euler&#x27;s theorem (homogeneous)","n = degree of homogeneity of u(x, y)","x ∂u/∂x + y ∂u/∂y = n u",1485,1525],[28,"Maxima/minima (2 variables)","","r = f<sub>xx</sub>, s = f<sub>xy</sub>, t = f<sub>yy</sub> at f<sub>x</sub> = f<sub>y</sub> = 0: rt − s² &gt; 0 and r &lt; 0 → max; r &gt; 0 → min; rt − s² &lt; 0 → saddle",1485,1525],[29,"Rolle&#x27;s &amp; Lagrange&#x27;s mean value","a &lt; c &lt; b","Rolle: f(a) = f(b) → f′(c) = 0; Lagrange: f′(c) = [f(b) − f(a)]/(b − a)",1485,1525],[30,"Taylor / Maclaurin series","","f(x) = f(a) + (x−a)f′(a) + (x−a)²f″(a)/2! + …; Maclaurin: a = 0",1485,1525],[31,"Jacobian","","J = ∂(u, v)/∂(x, y) = u<sub>x</sub>v<sub>y</sub> − u<sub>y</sub>v<sub>x</sub>",1485,1525],[32,"Convexity","","f″ &gt; 0 on an interval ⇒ f strictly convex: at most one local minimum (it is the global o